This product includes data from third parties under their own terms:

- GeoNames postal code data (https://www.geonames.org/), licensed under the
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 License
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Used for the ZIP-to-place
  tables in crates/doorplate/data/packs/ (see docs/packs/) and crates/doorplate/data/places/ (see
  docs/places.md), and for the postal place names in crates/doorplate/data/places/. The
  GeoNames data is provided "as is" and has been reformatted (upper-cased,
  de-accented, joined with Census names).
- US Census Bureau Gazetteer files and 2020 reference lists (public domain),
  used for place names, county subdivisions and counties in crates/doorplate/data/packs/ and
  crates/doorplate/data/places/.
- Florida public-record address data, used for observed city and ZIP pairs
  and street spellings in crates/doorplate/data/packs/fl/ (see
  docs/packs/fl.md). Public record; no attribution is required.
- usaddress test data (MIT, datamade), vendored in tests/external/usaddress/.
- National Address Database (NAD), US Department of Transportation
  (https://www.transportation.gov/gis/national-address-database), a work of the
  US federal government (public domain). Compiled with the US Census Bureau's
  Geography Division from the address data of its contributing state, local and
  tribal providers. Street, city, state and ZIP values are used, with invented
  house and unit numbers, in the benchmark suite in benchmarks/suite/ (see
  docs/benchmark-suite.md). The suite is for parser testing; it is not a list of
  real or deliverable addresses.
